
# JUSTICE AI
## COMPLETE FRONTEND DEVELOPMENT — MASTER PROJECT SPECIFICATION

You are an expert software architect, senior React developer, product designer, UI/UX engineer and quality assurance specialist.

Your task is to build a complete, premium, responsive and interactive legal technology web application named JUSTICE AI.

You must treat this as a serious legal-tech SaaS product intended for future real-world development, not as a simple website, static landing page or basic dashboard.

Build a complete application with multiple user roles, a professional design system, comprehensive navigation, functional interfaces, realistic demonstration data, reusable components and maintainable architecture.

The application will eventually be connected to a Python FastAPI backend, PostgreSQL database, authentication service, OCR engine, document processing system and AI-powered legal intelligence engine.

IMPORTANT: THIS DEVELOPMENT PHASE IS FRONTEND ONLY.

Do not configure a production database, external authentication provider, external AI API, OCR service, Google Maps API or live court integration.

Use local demonstration data and frontend state to implement the complete user experience.

Do not pretend that simulated features are genuinely operational.

==================================================
01. PRODUCT IDENTITY
==================================================

PRODUCT NAME:
JUSTICE AI

TAGLINE:
Understand Your Case. Make Informed Decisions.

ALTERNATIVE TAGLINE:
Clarity in Law. Intelligence in Action.

PRODUCT CATEGORY:
AI-Powered Legal Case Intelligence Platform.

TARGET MARKET:
India.

PRODUCT VISION:

JUSTICE AI is designed to simplify access to legal information by helping ordinary people understand complex legal documents, identify potentially important inconsistencies, analyse arguments, organise case information and discover suitable advocates.

The platform should act as an intelligent legal information assistant.

Its purpose is to bridge the gap between complicated legal information and ordinary people who may not have a legal background.

CORE OBJECTIVES:

1. Simplify complicated legal documents.
2. Extract important case information.
3. Identify potential contradictions across documents.
4. Explain arguments from different perspectives.
5. Organise evidence and case information.
6. Explore relevant Indian legal provisions.
7. Generate document-based case timelines.
8. Help users discover advocates.
9. Provide an accessible legal information experience.
10. Create a central workspace for managing legal cases.

The product must be neutral, transparent and privacy-conscious.

It must not claim to replace advocates, courts or professional legal advice.

